.TH OPENNHRP-HA 8 "18 Aug 2026" "" "OpenNHRP Documentation"

.SH NAME
opennhrp-ha \- managed pure mGRE multi-Hub coordinator

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opennhrp-ha
.BI "[-a " admin-socket "] -i " interface
.br
.B opennhrp-ha hub
.BI "[--state-dir " directory "] [-a " admin-socket "] [--control-socket " path "] [--listen-address " address "] [--health-target " address "]... [--debug]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opennhrp-ha
in Spoke mode consumes the OpenNHRP HA monitor stream and activates an
authenticated, READY Hub candidate. Neighbor replacement uses an internal
revision as a compare-and-swap guard; users do not configure a generation.
.PP
.B opennhrp-ha hub
loads the local member identity, manifest, authentication keys, and durable
cluster state from the managed directory. It accepts encrypted Invite joins
and replicates registrations and membership to as many as 32 Hubs over TCP
port 49002. New members are learners until their registration snapshot and
digest are synchronized.
.PP
Quorum depends on the number of active Hubs. Three or more active Hubs require
a majority whose reported term, Leader, and roles agree. A minority partition
self-fences. One or two Hubs use legacy availability-first election unless a
Manager Witness is activated for exactly two active Hubs.
.PP
In Manager Witness mode, a serviceable Leader needs its local vote plus either
a healthy agreeing peer vote or a valid Manager lease. Leases use a shared
epoch, nondecreasing term, strictly increasing sequence, and a maximum TTL of
3000 milliseconds. If both Hubs lose the Manager but remain healthy and fully
synchronized with each other, they can coordinate a fallback to legacy mode
after 30 seconds. A Hub partition cannot use this fallback.
.PP
The local mGRE interface must have IFF_UP for the Hub to remain serviceable.
When it goes down, the coordinator changes the local core to Standby, closes
Hub control connections, and rejects new connections. After the interface
returns or the coordinator restarts, the node remains isolated until it has
reconciled current term and Leader state with active members and satisfies the
current quorum policy.
.PP
When one or more
.B ha-health-target
directives are configured, each Hub sends ICMP Echo probes using system
routing policy. Any reply makes a round successful. Healthy intervals back
off through one, two, four, eight, and ten seconds. Three failed rounds isolate
a Hub; ten successful recovery rounds allow re-entry. With no target,
availability depends only on the mGRE interface.
.PP
Automatic failback targets the fixed Primary. After the Primary remains
authenticated and healthy for 120 seconds, the Backup transfers leadership
as soon as its registration match index and digest are synchronized. Transfer
failures retain the 300/900/1800 second retry backoff and 120 second probation.
.PP
The coordinator manages only pure IPv4 mGRE and NHRP state. It does not
configure IPsec, VICI, or XFRM. A Manager Witness is an external control-plane
client and does not participate in NHRP data forwarding.
.PP
Normally users do not start this program directly. An
.B opennhrp
configuration containing
.B enable-ha
starts Hub mode after the core administrative socket is ready. A Spoke starts
its per-interface coordinator after a traditional registering map receives a
valid managed Hub List. The parent daemon reaps and restarts failed
coordinators with bounded exponential backoff.
.PP
Membership updates are synchronized into the local core with a
managed-state-only reload. This refreshes Hub List, authentication, term,
commit index, and Leader state without reparsing the main configuration file.

.SH OPTIONS
.BI "-a " admin-socket
.RS
Use an alternate OpenNHRP administrative socket.
.RE

.BI "-i " interface
.RS
Run the Spoke coordinator for this mGRE interface.
.RE

.BI "--state-dir " directory
.RS
Override the default managed state directory
.IR /etc/opennhrp/ha .
This is intended for isolated tests and explicitly selected instances.
.RE

.BI "--control-socket " path
.RS
Override the Hub coordinator management socket. The default is
.IR /var/run/opennhrp-ha.socket .
.RE

.BI "--listen-address " address
.RS
Override the default Hub listener address 0.0.0.0. The port remains 49002.
This controls only the local bind address; the configured and authenticated
observed endpoint list controls peer connection attempts.
.RE

.BI "--health-target " address
.RS
Configure an IPv4 ICMP Echo health target passed by the supervised parent.
Users normally configure
.B ha-health-target
in
.BR opennhrp.conf (5)
instead of invoking this option directly.
.RE

.B --debug
.RS
Copy coordinator election, quorum, health, replication, transfer, and timeout
events to the system log. The supervised parent enables this automatically
when
.B opennhrp
runs with
.BR -v .
.RE

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR opennhrp (8),
.BR opennhrpctl (8),
.BR opennhrp.conf (5)
